---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { AUTHOR_NAME } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`Privacy Policy | ${AUTHOR_NAME}`}
			description="How this site handles data: hosting, comments, and why there is no cookie banner."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main class="prose">
			<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
			<p class="meta">
				This applies regardless of the site's language, since the site is operated from Germany
				and GDPR applies to the operator, not the visitor.
			</p>

			<h2>Responsible party</h2>
			<p>
				Sebastian Koch, Industriestraße 29, 82194 Gröbenzell, Germany.{' '}
				<a href="mailto:sebastian.koch@consos.de">sebastian.koch@consos.de</a>. See the{' '}
				<a href="/imprint">imprint</a> for full details.
			</p>

			<h2>Hosting</h2>
			<p>
				This site is hosted on Cloudflare's network. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes
				technical connection data for every request, such as IP address, browser type, and
				timestamp, in order to deliver the site and to protect it against abuse. This happens
				automatically and is not something this site's code controls directly. Cloudflare acts as
				a data processor here and publishes its own{' '}
				<a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
					>privacy policy</a
				> and data processing terms, including safeguards for international data transfers.
			</p>

			<h2>Fonts</h2>
			<p>
				This site uses IBM Plex fonts, downloaded once at build time and served from this site's
				own domain. Your browser never contacts Google or any other font provider when you visit
				this site.
			</p>

			<h2>Comments</h2>
			<p>
				Articles have an optional comment section. If you post a comment, the name you choose to
				enter, the comment text, and the time of posting are stored in a Cloudflare D1 database so
				the comment can be displayed. I do not store your IP address alongside comments. New
				comments are held in a private moderation queue and only become publicly visible after I
				review them; rejected comments are deleted rather than published.
			</p>
			<p>
				The comment form is protected by Cloudflare Turnstile, a captcha alternative that helps
				block automated spam. The Turnstile script only loads on article pages that show a comment
				form, not sitewide, and only runs when you interact with the form. Your browser sends your
				IP address to Cloudflare as part of that verification; this site does not receive or store
				it. Turnstile is used because it is necessary to provide the commenting feature you are
				actively using, not for tracking.
			</p>

			<h2>No analytics, no advertising</h2>
			<p>
				This site runs no analytics, advertising, or marketing scripts, and sets no tracking
				cookies. Because of that, there is no cookie consent banner: nothing non-essential is
				loaded that would require your consent under the ePrivacy rules. If that ever changes,
				this page and a consent mechanism will be updated accordingly.
			</p>

			<h2>External links</h2>
			<p>
				Where articles link to external sites (for example, Microsoft's documentation), those
				sites have their own privacy policies that this policy does not cover.
			</p>

			<h2>Your rights</h2>
			<p>
				Under GDPR you have the right to access, correct, or delete data concerning you, to
				restrict or object to its processing, and to data portability. If you posted a comment and
				want it edited or removed, email{' '}
				<a href="mailto:sebastian.koch@consos.de">sebastian.koch@consos.de</a> with a link to the
				page and I will take care of it. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data
				protection supervisory authority.
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	main.prose {
		width: 720px;
		max-width: calc(100% - 2em);
		margin: auto;
		padding: 3em 1em;
		color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
	}
</style>
